<h2>Spring 2025</h2>
<p>It&#039;s been a few rotations of the earth since I sent an update and during those rotations, I&#039;ve had the opportunity to take part in a number of training events in which I presented <a href="https://tmm.io">TMM.io</a> and <a href="https://issuesiface.com">other</a> <a href="https://thelife.com">ways</a> that we serve the global ministry.</p>
<h3>Unlock:Thailand</h3>
<p>Phuket, Thailand in December is quite amazing. It was a last minute trip involving 3 flights over 2 days, which left me jet lagged to a point I only hit the beach for 5 minutes. I&#039;m really not made for a lot of heat.</p>
<p>This training conference had numerous attendees from &quot;secure&quot; countries. These countries are talked about often when discussing the persecuted church so I can&#039;t list them here. What I can say is it is humbling to hear stories of our staff fleeing their own families due to the ramifications of not just being a Christian, but telling others about him. The consequences levied by the family is often worse than what the authorities would do.</p>
<p>As a number of the attendees were new to Digital Strategies, we started from scratch. We talked about content strategy, how to do followup in a digital world, and analytics. We also dove into how to create content with Artificial Intelligence.</p>
<h3>Unlock:Uninterested</h3>
<p>In March I took another red-eye flight to the amazing city of Tokyo. Riding a train from the airport into the city is an experience as you go from small homes and fields into an area where you can&#039;t see the tops of buildings. The Tokyo metro area has around the same amount of people as all of Canada was something I kept in mind as I experienced crowds in the train stations and in the areas of the city like the scramble crossing.</p>
<p>The other thing I kept in mind was that the vast majority of people in Japan (and Canada) would say they are uninterested in Jesus and Christianity in general. <a href="https://audiencemap.cru.org/map/">Our audience map</a> is the guide we use when we try and figure out how to share Jesus and this part of the map is where the Spirit needs to really spark curiosity.</p>
<p></p>
